pi divided by B we get PI  divided by 1/2 which equals 2 pi ok so  what's actually happening we're not  actually dividing the x-values by 2 were  actually multiplying them by 2 it  actually has the opposite effect on the  graph but you can just use this formula  pi divided by the coefficient in front  of X ok that will give you your period  now this is one thing that I want to  mention to you is  when you go to graph this take that  period 2pi and cut it in half and the  reason is it because half the graph is  to the right of the y-axis and half to  the left so what you want to do even  though the period is 2pi is divide this  by two so that's going to be one pi and  over here this is going to be negative  one pi but that gives you a period of  2pi right so your asymptotes are going  to be right here okay just like in the  parent function and what I like to do is  find these halfway points these Midway  points so I would take PI and divide it  by two again so that gives you PI over 2  and negative PI over 2 and then all you  want to do is plot these key points so  we've got 1 0 and negative 1 and that's  our graph ok let's look at another  example here we have y equals 2 times  tangent of 4x so again we're gonna look  at the period it's pi divided by 4 okay  so we're going to do is we're going to  take that period PI over 4 we're gonna  cut it in half because half's on the  right side of the y axis halves on the  left so this is going to be over here at  PI over 8 and negative PI over 8  effectively giving us a period of PI  over 4 are you with me so far  okay so I'm going to draw in the  asymptotes I'm going to take that PI  over 8 I'm going to cut it in half again  so we're at PI over 16 and negative PI  over 16 but what's different about this  function is you see the two here the two  in front of the tangents going to  stretch the graph by two times so  instead of being at 1 we're gonna now be  out here at 2 instead of being at  negative 1 we're gonna be down here at  negative 2 so I'm taking these values  here and I'm multiplying by 2 its  stretching it vertically but 0 times 2  is still 0 so it's still gonna cross  right through at the origin there and  there's the graph now another question  that students sometimes have is they get  a little bit Wiggly with this line here  and what you can do you can think about  when you graph this on this side of the  graph it's what they call concave up  it's like a c-shape up so it's curving  this way up like a C up and when on this  side of the graph it's concave down it's  like a c-shape down so what you can  sometimes do instead of just trying to  graph it like this is start from the  origin do that part like a c-shape down  and then on this side graph it like  this and graph of see shape up and  that'll give you a nice curve you can  also think of it as like y equals x  cubed if you're familiar with that graph  let's look at one last example and  that's this one here y equals tangent X  minus PI over four here you can see the  PI over four is actually going to pick  up the graph it's going to shift it  right PI over four if this was plus PI  over four it would be shifting it to the  left PI over four so it has the opposite  effect on the graph when you multiply or  divide that's going to be stretching or  compressing when you add or subtract  that's gonna be picking picking up and  shifting or translating okay so let me  just show you this one real quick and  then we'll wrap up this video but here  you can see the D value the number in  front of the ax is one so if we use our  formula pi divided by b pi divided by  one is just going to be pi but i'm going  to take that period and divide it in  half because half's on the right side of  the y axis halves on the left and then  i'm gonna divide it in half again that's  PI over 4 and negative PI over 4 and I'm  gonna draw on the asymptotes okay just  like we did in the previous examples and  then we're gonna draw in our key points  one zero and negative one and so our  graph looks like this right now the PI  over four is gonna pick everything up  even the asymptotes and shift it right  PI over 4 you can see the scales PI over  4 so it's just going to be one step to  the right notice also that the  asymptotes are gonna shift one step to  the right so now our new graph is going  to be like this ok there's a lot going  on here in this graph but you can see  everything's going to shift right one  steps like this so there's our new graph  so I hope this video helped you  understand how to graph tangents better  subscribe to the channel check out some  of my other many videos and I look  forward to seeing you in the next video  I'll talk to you soon
 

